BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Black Angel (1946)
DTSTART:20260214T030000Z
DTEND:20260214T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260214T030000Z
UID:cHBA7A3UPu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nA man is sentenced to die for th
 e murder of an actress\, but the man’s wife (June Vincent) won’t give 
 up trying to prove his innocence. She enlists the aid of a pianist on the 
 skids (Dan Duryea) hoping to find the real killer. A slick adaptation of a
  sordid Cornell Woolrich yarn.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events
 /noir-city/black-angel\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Nora Prentiss (1946)
DTSTART:20260214T203000Z
DTEND:20260214T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260214T203000Z
UID:lqsg9XXK6k
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 131 mins (2h11m)\n\nA neglected classic! Richard Tal
 bot (Kent Smith) is the squarest doctor you’ll ever meet\, but he’s so
  taken by San Francisco nightclub singer Nora Prentiss (Ann Sheridan) that
  he decides to throw his life away in the hopes of winning her over.\n\nht
 tps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/nora-prentiss\n\nEstimate
 d start: 12:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: The Man I Love (1946)
DTSTART:20260215T000000Z
DTEND:20260215T021500Z
DTSTAMP:20260215T000000Z
UID:NjpR41REOr
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nA coast-to-coast road trip throu
 gh a world of atmospheric nightclubs\, tenements\, and backlot streets\, 
 this majestic melodrama is part noir\, part soap opera\, and pure Hollywoo
 d magic. As flinty chanteuse Petey Brown\, Ida Lupino is at the apex of 
 her big-screen glamour.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-c
 ity/the-man-i-love\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Gilda (1946)
DTSTART:20260215T030000Z
DTEND:20260215T052500Z
DTSTAMP:20260215T030000Z
UID:KCWZ63oIob
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 130 mins (2h10m)\n\nThe sexual tension flies when Jo
 hnny Farrell (Glenn Ford) accepts a gig with sinister casino owner Ballin 
 Mundson (George Macready) only to reignite a romance with Mundson’s bomb
 shell wife\, Gilda (Rita Hayworth). Cue betrayal\, innuendo-spiked dialogu
 e\, and Hayworth’s legendary “Put the Blame on Mame” performance.\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/gilda\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: A Man Called Adam (1966)
DTSTART:20260215T203000Z
DTEND:20260215T224500Z
DTSTAMP:20260215T203000Z
UID:8NICxyLRSL
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 119 mins (1h59m)\n\nSammy Davis\, Jr. like you’ve 
 never seen him before! Davis’ portrayal of Adam\, the tortured cornetist
  alternating between self-sabotage and rotten luck\, remains as startling 
 today as when it was released. Leo Penn keeps his directorial choices for 
 this unrelentingly bleak noir simple yet powerful.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /programs-and-events/noir-city/a-man-called-adam\n\nEstimated start: 12:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Young Man With a Horn (1950)
DTSTART:20260215T234000Z
DTEND:20260216T021000Z
DTSTAMP:20260215T234000Z
UID:TRD06igH6F
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 132 mins (2h12m)\n\nA study in wasted potential. Kir
 k Douglas is a trumpet prodigy who lives for his music\, but his arrogance
  (and alcohol) threaten to ruin him. Doris Day is the loyal singer whose l
 ove is unrequited and Lauren Bacall is the woman he craves but can’t com
 prehend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/young-man-w
 ith-a-horn\n\nEstimated start: 15:55
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: The Man With the Golden Arm (1955)
DTSTART:20260216T030000Z
DTEND:20260216T053500Z
DTSTAMP:20260216T030000Z
UID:leNwQjlmkc
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 139 mins (2h19m)\n\nOne of the first noir films to e
 xplore hard drugs\, strikingly directed by Preminger and startlingly raw i
 n its depiction of dependency. Frank Sinatra\, earning an Oscar nomination
  for his performance\, is heartbreaking as the golden-armed drummer who po
 ssesses more charisma than willpower.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and
 -events/noir-city/the-man-with-the-golden-arm\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Pete Kelly's Blues (1955)
DTSTART:20260217T020000Z
DTEND:20260217T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260217T020000Z
UID:wDfagCtKqC
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 115 mins (1h55m)\n\nJack Webb stars (and directs!) a
 s Prohibition-era bandleader Pete Kelly who refuses to bow to a local boot
 legger. With Janet Leigh as the flapper complicating Pete’s life and voc
 al powerhouses Peggy Lee (who earned a 1956 Best Supporting Actress nod) a
 nd Ella Fitzgerald.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/
 pete-kellys-blues\n\nEstimated start: 18:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Love Me or Leave Me (1955)
DTSTART:20260217T044500Z
DTEND:20260217T071500Z
DTSTAMP:20260217T044500Z
UID:6WgEWLdZXc
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 132 mins (2h12m)\n\nThe life of singer Ruth Etting g
 ets the full noir treatment. Doris Day gives a powerhouse performance as E
 tting\, both dramatically and vocally\, while James Cagney chews the scene
 ry as the gangster who refuses to let her out of his grasp. 1956 Oscar win
 ner - “Best Writing\, Motion Picture Story”.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/p
 rograms-and-events/noir-city/love-me-or-leave-me\n\nEstimated start: 21:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Sweet Smell of Success (1957)
DTSTART:20260218T020000Z
DTEND:20260218T041500Z
DTSTAMP:20260218T020000Z
UID:0jQ3tGS9vD
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nA cinematic diamond! Burt Lancas
 ter is gossip columnist J.J. Hunsecker who makes and breaks careers\, and 
 Tony Curtis is publicist Sidney Falco who will sell his soul for a whiff o
 f the same power. The definitive cinematic statement on the dangers of med
 ia corruption.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/sweet
 -smell-of-success\n\nEstimated start: 18:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: King Creole (1958)
DTSTART:20260218T044500Z
DTEND:20260218T071000Z
DTSTAMP:20260218T044500Z
UID:nFmrXDYy9F
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 126 mins (2h06m)\n\nElvis Presley delivers the actin
 g performance of his career as a New Orleans nightclub singer who is dragg
 ed back into a life of crime by the crooked businessman who discovered him
 . Carolyn Jones haunts as the call girl who gets caught between warring sh
 ow-biz factions.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/kin
 g-creole\n\nEstimated start: 21:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Thunder Road (1958)
DTSTART:20260219T020000Z
DTEND:20260219T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260219T020000Z
UID:52QTTrRImn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nHigh octane on a low budget! Rob
 ert Mitchum is a moonshiner who runs afoul of big-city gangsters and feder
 al agents\, and his real-life son\, James\, portrays the kid brother wanti
 ng in on the action. Mitchum’s most personal film – he wrote the story
 \, co-produced the film\, and co-wrote two of the film’s songs including
  “The Ballad of Thunder Road.”\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-ev
 ents/noir-city/thunder-road\n\nEstimated start: 18:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: To Have and Have Not (1944)
DTSTART:20260219T044500Z
DTEND:20260219T065000Z
DTSTAMP:20260219T044500Z
UID:sxMA7kLdZN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nHumphrey Bogart is the sneakily 
 heroic fisherman. Lauren Bacall is the songbird who steals his heart -- an
 d every scene in which she appears. Ground zero for one of Hollywood’s m
 ost beloved couples\, and proof that director Hawks could salvage Ernest H
 emingway’s self-described “worst” novel.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/pro
 grams-and-events/noir-city/to-have-and-have-not\n\nEstimated start: 21:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Kansas City (1996)
DTSTART:20260220T014500Z
DTEND:20260220T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260220T014500Z
UID:BtxkcMDG6T
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 128 mins (2h08m)\n\nJennifer Jason Leigh plays a Jea
 n Harlow-obsessed housewife who abducts the spouse of a local politician b
 efore the 1934 Democratic primary election. She goes on a wild ride\, and 
 so will you courtesy of Altman’s spirited recreations of the 1930s jazz 
 scene.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/kansas-city\n
 \nEstimated start: 18:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Round Midnight (1986)
DTSTART:20260220T044500Z
DTEND:20260220T072500Z
DTSTAMP:20260220T044500Z
UID:inxpsOBox0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 143 mins (2h23m)\n\nA troubled saxophonist (Dexter G
 ordon) cleans up his act in 1950s Paris\, but finds temptation lurking on 
 every street corner when he returns to reestablish his life in New York. C
 o-starring Herbie Hancock\, 1987 Academy Award winner Best Music\, Origina
 l Score for the film.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-cit
 y/round-midnight\n\nEstimated start: 21:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
